  "result": "I fixed the spurious notifications in `src/lib/mentions.ts`. I haven't run the test suite or added a test.\n\n`extractMentions` scanned the raw comment body. The helper `withoutCode`, which strips fenced blocks and inline code spans, was defined but never called. Any `@word` inside a code block was treated as a mention, so a shell snippet notified whoever had that handle. `extractMentions` now scans `withoutCode(body)`, so mentions inside code no longer notify anyone and mentions outside it still do.\n\nI also extended `withoutCode` to strip `~~~` fences as well as backtick fences. An unclosed fence now hides everything after it.\n\nI left `highlightMentions` alone. It still wraps `@handle` inside code blocks in the styled mention span when the comment is displayed, though it no longer triggers a notification there.",
